	An announcement has been made in net.lang.st80 of the availability
of a Smalltalk-like system, called Little Smalltalk.  The source for this
system can be obtained from the University of Arizona for a nominal fee.
One of the objectives in developing this system was to make available to
students (particularly our students) a Smalltalk - like language that did
not require the special purpose hardware of the Xerox systems.  Little
Smalltalk requires only a Unix system with standard ascii terminals.
More details can be found in net.lang.st80 - see you there!


